the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the season is *a value*.
    the number of guests is *a value*.
    the guests with children is *a value*.
    the dish is *a text*.
    the guest count is *a number*.
    the guests with children two is *a truth value*.
    the season two is *a text*.
    the dish or null is *a text*.
    the guests with children two or null is *a truth value*.

the templates are:
    the beverages include *a text*.
    the beverages are listed.
    the beverages for *a text* and *a truth value* is *a second text* under table beverages.
    the dish for *a text* and *a number* is *a second text* under table dish.

the table beverages is, with all matches:
    desired dish                                                          | guests with children | beverages
    "Spareribs"                                                           | any                  | "Aecht Schlenkerla Rauchbier"
    "Stew"                                                                | any                  | "Guiness"
    "Roastbeef"                                                           | any                  | "Bordeaux"
    "Steak" or "Dry Aged Gourmet Steak" or "Light Salad and a nice Steak" | any                  | "Pinot Noir"
    any                                                                   | true                 | "Apple Juice"
    any                                                                   | any                  | "Water"

the table dish is, with unique match:
    season                         | guest count   | desired dish
    "Fall"                         | <= 8          | "Spareribs"
    "Winter"                       | <= 8          | "Roastbeef"
    "Spring"                       | <= 4          | "Dry Aged Gourmet Steak"
    "Spring"                       | >= 5 and <= 8 | "Steak"
    "Fall" or "Winter" or "Spring" | > 8           | "Stew"
    "Summer"                       | any           | "Light Salad and a nice Steak"

the knowledge base dinnerdecisions includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/dinnerDecisions.dmn".

the dish or null is the dish, as stated in the model at decision Beverages.

rule beverages_2 with provenance the model at decision Beverages:
the dish or null is null if
    it is not the case that the dish is a text.

the guests with children two or null is the guests with children two, as stated in the model at decision Beverages.

rule beverages_4 with provenance the model at decision Beverages:
the guests with children two or null is null if
    it is not the case that the guests with children two is a truth value.

rule beverages_5 with provenance the model at decision Beverages:
the beverages include a text if
    the beverages for the dish or null and the guests with children two or null is the text under table beverages.

rule dish_1 with provenance the model at decision Dish:
the dish is a text if
    the dish for the season two and the guest count is the text under table dish.

